            "page_count": null,
            "download_url": null,
            "author_id": null,
            "opinion_text": "\n28 So. 3d 1015 (2010)\nJessica KELLY\nv.\nAlbert MANUEL, et al.\nNo. 2010-CC-0247.\nSupreme Court of Louisiana.\nMarch 12, 2010.\n*1016 Granted. The trial court erred in finding plaintiffs claims for penalties and attorney fees should not be included in calculating the amount of plaintiffs cause of action for purposes of La.Code Civ. P. art. 1732(1). See Cambridge Corner Corp. v. Menard, 525 So. 2d 527, 530 (La.1988). Accordingly, the judgment of the trial court striking relator's jury trial is reversed, and the case is remanded to the trial court for further proceedings.\n",
            "ocr": false,
            "opinion_id": 1595081
          }
        ],
